-- title:
--   Invariant chart element in no Igusa valuation ring of K₀
-- statement:
--   **Setting and data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$ (`hq2`), let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`). The level group $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is (`hH₁`) the intersection of `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units that are congruent to $1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$.
--
--   On the side of the constants, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for which $q$ is a non-unit (`hA`, the predicate `LiesOverPrime`). $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — the subfield of the Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'` of $j$ — and `hW` asserts that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of supersingular places: places $w$ that are rational (the structure map to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of $j$-invariants such that every elliptic curve with that invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$. A distinguished element $s \in W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` places the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full modular function field of level $M'$ (generated by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid M'$) inside `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of level $(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$. The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of the former field over $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `integers` meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$, together with a map on places preserving degrees and the orders of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that a Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in the base-changed field lies in `R₀.integers` and that its $R_0$-residue is its coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Next, $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$ (`hπ`); write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$. The local hypotheses on the constants are: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), $A_0$ is henselian (`hhens`), its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`). Auxiliary arithmetic data: a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`); an element $\xi \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`); an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hϖtA`) with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`); an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (`hKb`) and a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose membership agrees with that of $A$ (`hAb`), with maximal ideal generated by a non-zero $\varpi_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`); and the tameness hypothesis `htame` that the natural number $(\ell_g - 1)/2$ is a unit in $A_0$.
--
--   On the curve side, $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$ equal (`hKℓ`) to the $k_0$-base change of the function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁`, carrying an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$; $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is non-zero and equals (`hjℓ`) the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb k₀ jq` of the $q$-expansion of $j$. Write $R =$ `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` for the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$. The ideal $y \subseteq R$ is maximal (`hy`) and contains the image of $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: every ring homomorphism from $R$ to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y$ sends the class `jChartFin` of $j_\ell$ into `ssJSet q Ω`. Moreover (`hjC`) the element `jqNModC k₀ q`, the $q$-expansion of $j$ in the variable $\mathsf q^q$, lies in $K_\ell$ (`hjK`) and in $R$, and (`ha₀y`) its difference with the image of an element $a_0 \in A_0$ lies in $y$. An element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ has image $\varpi_t$ in $k_0$ (`hϖt'`), and an integer $m \ge 1$ (`hm1`) satisfies $\pi_0^{\,m} = \varpi_t' w$ for a unit $w$ of $A_0$ (`hm`). Further data: an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t \subseteq K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$; an integer $n \ge 1$ (`hn1`) with $n \mid q+1$ (`hnq`) and $n =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (`hn`), the width $12$ or $1$ according as the $j$-value of $s$ vanishes or not, divided by the ramification index `placeRamificationJ M' s`; an element $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`) and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁` (`hτ₀`) — the $q$-expansion condition comparing $\tau_0 x$ with the $\gamma_0^{-1}$-translate of a ratio of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ under any embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ — and which preserves $W_t$ (`hτ₀W`); and an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^{\,n} = 1$ (`hζc`) and $\zeta_c^{\,k}-1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$ (`hζcprim`).
--
--   **Compatibility, orbit and rigid-chart hypotheses.** The hypothesis `hover` states that $y$ is the point of the chart cut out by the place $s$: for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which has non-negative order at every place of the base-changed field at which $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for which `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$ and in $R$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of $g$ and $c$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hOrbit` states that every maximal ideal $y'$ of $R$ containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same compatibility condition is linked to $y$ by a level automorphism: there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ which maps $R$ into itself and satisfies $f \in y \iff \tau f \in y'$ for all $f \in R$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hS1` (a conjunction of clauses, summarised here) describes the pair $(B_t, W_t)$: $R \subseteq B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the field of fractions of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$, and $B_t/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, and is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal, and $y$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ to $R$; for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection of $B_t$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) of that residue field whose zero locus is the maximal ideal of $W_t$, which is $A_0$-equivariant and which intertwines the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W_t$ with the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of elements $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the scalar $c$ being non-trivial for non-trivial automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)$ and realisable with trivial matrix part by a further level automorphism; $B_t$ is stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is reached from the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by such an automorphism; and an element of $B_t$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ after every level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hR7` (a long conjunction, summarised here) describes the special fibre: $\tau_0$ has exact order $n$ on $B_t$, every level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power of $\tau_0$, the set `ends` has $q+1$ elements, is permuted transitively by the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W_t$, is fixed elementwise by $\tau_0$, and distinct ends are separated by an element that is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; there is a level-stable finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$ contained in every end, each end being a localisation of $B_c$; an end whose image under a level automorphism lies in $W_t$ forces that automorphism to preserve $W_t$; each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is a noetherian local ring containing $R$ and meeting $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, has residue field generated by the constants, and its adic completion is isomorphic to the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the completion of $A_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{\,m}$, the isomorphism matching constants, carrying two elements $c_x, c_y$ of $O$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{\,m}u$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, sending the difference of `jqNModC k₀ q` and $a_0$ to a unit times $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$, and conjugating $\tau_0$ into an automorphism $\theta_0$ which multiplies $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; each end also carries a discrete valuation ring $W_x$ containing it and $R$, with constants $A_0$, maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, with $j_\ell$ and `jqNModC k₀ q` residually transcendental over the constants, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, recovering $y$ on $R$, and separating the given end from the other ends and from their level translates; and a level-stable finite-type subalgebra $B_x \subseteq B_t \cap O$ with no poles where $j_\ell$ is regular, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$, containing an element that lies in no valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$, $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal, $j_\ell$ residually transcendental, and not containing all of $O$. A final clause of `hR7` is a dichotomy: a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$ containing $R$ and with $y$ inside its maximal ideal either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends.
--
--   The hypothesis `hR9` provides an element $b \in B_t$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ whose constants are $A_0$, for which $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, and for which $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental over the constants (no monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$). The hypothesis `hR10` provides, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $R$ containing $\pi_0$ which is not linked to $y$ by any level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, an element $b \in B_t$ which, for every such $\gamma$ and level automorphism $\tau$, lies outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ containing $R$ whose maximal ideal contains the $\tau$-pullback of $y''$.
--
--   **The invariant block.** Finally, $G$ is the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated (`hG`) by the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; $K_0$ is the intermediate field of $K_\ell/k_0$ equal to the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ is the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ consisting (`hB₀`) of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$; and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ whose elements are those lying in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists an element $b$ of $K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$, such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ the following holds: if an element $x$ of $k_0$ lies in $A$ precisely when its image in $K_0$ lies in $V$; if $\pi_0$, whenever its image lies in $V$, lies in the maximal ideal of $V$; and if the $q$-expansion `coeffEmb k₀ jq` lies in $K_\ell$, the resulting element lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and no monic polynomial $p \in k_0[X]$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$ takes, at that element, a value lying in the maximal ideal of $V$ (the value being assumed to lie in $V$) — then $b \notin V$.
--
--   This is the descent step of the $q = 2$, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-frame analysis of the supersingular special fibre: from a rigid chart upstairs on the curve of level $(q^2M', H_1)$ it produces an element of the $G$-invariant subalgebra $B_0$ of the fixed field $K_0$ that generates a pole at every Igusa-type valuation ring of $K_0$ (constants $A$, uniformiser $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal, $j$ residually transcendental). It is used in the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation ring, affine chart and node data at level $M'$, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
